Implement user story SKY-002-impl: Implement SkyscannerClient class with mock mode and error handling

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.ts exporting SkyscannerClient, SearchParams, and FlightResult. Client resolves apiKey from constructor or RAPIDAPI_KEY env var, calls Skyscanner RapidAPI via global fetch, throws on HTTP errors and parse errors without leaking the key, and supports opt-in mock mode via MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true'.

## Acceptance Criteria
- new SkyscannerClient({ apiKey: 'k' }) succeeds; new SkyscannerClient({}) with RAPIDAPI_KEY unset throws Error whose message contains 'apiKey' (case-insensitive)
- Constructor param apiKey takes precedence over RAPIDAPI_KEY env var when both are present
- searchFlights returns Promise<FlightResult[]>; each element has price(number), currency(string), airline(string), departure(string), arrival(string), duration(number), stops(number)
- searchFlights rejects with Error whose message includes the numeric HTTP status code when API returns 4xx or 5xx
- searchFlights rejects with Error when response body cannot be parsed into FlightResult[]
- No Error thrown by SkyscannerClient contains the resolved apiKey value in its message
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true', searchFlights returns a deterministic FlightResult[] with ≥1 element and zero fetch calls
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API is unset or any value ≠ 'true', searchFlights invokes fetch; a fetch failure never falls back to mock data





